{
  "analysis": "Design says (S19, docs/query_serving/listen_notify_design.md at the pinned commit): LISTEN is served by one dedicated PostgreSQL connection per multipooler and one gRPC NotificationStream per client session from the gateway to the pooler; 'if the gRPC stream ... breaks (e.g., multipooler restart), the stream is automatically re-established with a 2-second backoff', and only notifications sent during a reconnect window are lost (documented limitation). G10: notifications sent after recovery are delivered. System did: each W6 listener (one per gateway, one LISTEN per connection) kept a single session for the whole run and received every notification committed before the first fault and none committed after it, through the rest of the workload and the 11 s tail; C8 judged only NOTIFYs committed after the listener's first successful operation post-recovery and outside every fault window (ADR-0030) and all of them were missed (notify-not-resumed); misses inside reconnect windows are the observation notify-window-loss. Mechanism, from the source at e3cbdbb (go/services/multigateway/poolergateway/notification_adapter.go): a session's stream is built and rebuilt only inside update(), i.e. when the client issues LISTEN or UNLISTEN (restartLocked → startLocked re-subscribes the active channels); recvLoop returns on a stream error after posting it to a channel read only by the next update; nothing re-establishes the stream otherwise. After a failover an unbroken stream stays on the old leader's pooler, which is now a standby where nothing is notified (PostgreSQL refuses LISTEN during recovery). A client that LISTENs once therefore stops receiving notifications after the first pooler restart or leader change (LIM-37). Seed 3: first fault F6 (graceful switchover) at 10.4 s, n2 → n1; listeners received 600 notifications (before the fault) and missed 3 322; C8: notify-not-resumed after recovery, 6 044 notify-window-loss. The two earlier attempts of this cell were INVALID by a harness defect in F6's heal (fixed in 2b968c5; NOTES §11) and count toward nothing. Minimized: F6 alone, 22.5 s, all clients; replays 1/5 FAIL with notify-not-resumed (INTERMITTENT): with the drained pooler restarted only after it exits, the loss after a lone switchover does not always reach the judged interval.",
